// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 15-function-semantics
// facility: rule.fn.bind-param (D-0049: an exclusive reference for a shared parameter is reborrowed shared at the call, D-0219, CHG-0258); conf.shared-param-given-reborrowed-exclusive
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (static)
//
// `r` is passed to a shared parameter while `r2`, an exclusive reborrow of
// it, lives. Binding the parameter first borrows shared through `r`
// (D-0049), and that borrow meets `r2`: the call faults, at the call.
// `coby` bound ordinary calls' parameters without the reborrow, and the
// conflict surfaced at the read inside `peek`, a line `cobc` did not
// report. Found by the model (D-0219).
//
// D-0282: the static pass rejects this program before it runs (it was found
// at run time before): `peek` reads `*r` through argument 1 while `r2`
// still borrows `*r`.

import std;

fn peek(ref<i32, shared> p) : i32
{
    *p
}

fn main()
{
    i32 x = 1;
    auto r = &mut x;
    auto r2 = &mut *r;
    printf("%v\n", peek(r));
    *r2 = 2;
}
